# Content Layer

`src/content/` is the only place portfolio copy lives. Components read from it;
they never contain a project name, metric, date or paragraph inline.

| Module          | Owns                                                  |
| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `site.ts`       | Identity, contact, socials, nav, headline figures     |
| `work.ts`       | Flagship projects + the public `archive`              |
| `stack.ts`      | The four disciplines behind the section 03 explorer   |
| `story.ts`      | Timeline chapters and which schematic plate each uses |
| `signals.ts`    | Proof claims and the credential ledger                |
| `production.ts` | Shipped apps and the pipeline strip                   |

## Accuracy bar

Every number is a real number. No invented metrics, clients, testimonials or dates.
If a figure can't be sourced to actual work, it doesn't ship. When a claim is
approximate, say so in the copy (`1k–10k`, `20+`) rather than inventing precision.

## Adding a field

Extend the exported type first, then fill every existing record. Optional fields
should be genuinely optional in the UI:

```ts
export type WorkItem = {
  // ...
  href?: string;                       // private work has no public link
  visibility: "private" | "public";
};
```

```tsx
{item.href
  ? <a href={item.href}>View ↗</a>
  : <span className="label text-whisper">Private repository</span>}
```

Blog posts are Markdown in `content/blog/` with `title`, `description`, `date`,
`category`, `tags` and `readTime` frontmatter — parsed by `src/lib/blog.ts`.
